cs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/test-plan.md:143:| 0 — rename + logging | renamed tree compiles; logging skeleton present; existing tests reference new names and fail only on logging-not-implemented | suite green under renamed vocabulary; TC-5.1a–5.5a pass. (`tool_call_summary` is renamed-but-retained here; its removal is Chunk 2.) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/test-plan.md:145:| 2 — tool-result tiers + `tool_call_summary` removal | tier-gate + removal tests red (`tool_call_summary` still present) | TC-2.1a–2.8a pass; `tool_call_summary` gone from kind set/registry/`PART_PLANS`/provider |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/test-plan.md:148:| 5 — runtime typing | typed-block projection tests red | TC-6.1a–6.3a pass |\npackages/lhc/src/shared/inspect.ts:78:  // Counts by owner, form kind, and operational state (AC-4.1), assembled\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:134:    expect(readDerivedForms(threadM).map((form) => form.state)).toEqual([\"pending\"]);\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:138:    expect(readDerivedForms(threadB).map((form) => form.state)).toEqual([\"ready\"]);\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:144:    expect(readDerivedForms(threadM).map((form) => form.state)).toEqual([\"ready\"]);\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:165:    expect(readDerivedForms(threadM).map((form) => form.state)).toEqual([\"pending\"]);\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:194:      (form) => form.subjectId === \"m3\" && form.derivationType === \"tool_result_summary\",\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:198:      (form) => form.subjectId === \"m1\" && form.derivationType === \"smoothed_prompt\",\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:207:    expect(result.value.cleared.map(formKey)).not.toContain(\"message/m2/tool_call_summary\");\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:208:    expect(result.value.queued.map((item) => item.kind)).not.toContain(\"tool_call_summary\");\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:216:      (form) => form.subjectId === \"m1\" && form.derivationType === \"smoothed_prompt\",\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:247:    // The form derived on the second attempt — the retry actually ran.\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:278:    // Exactly one attempt — the retry has NOT run before eligible_at, the form\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:393:    expect(readDerivedForms(filePath).map((f) => f.derivationType)).not.toContain(\"tool_call_summary\");\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:408:    expect(deleted.value.cleared.map(formKey)).not.toContain(\"message/m2/tool_call_summary\");\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:409:    expect(deleted.value.queued.map((q) => q.kind)).not.toContain(\"tool_call_summary\");\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:442:    // Delete m3 (the tool_result) while its summary item is claimed. Its own form\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:457:    // Tombstone intact: m3 is gone from the live read and its summary form was\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:15:**Vocabulary (this epic settles it).** A **derivation** is the stored result of producing a representation of existing content — a smoothed prompt, a tool-result summary, a turn rendering, a chunk summary. To **derive** is the act. A **derivation type** names which one. A derivation carries a **state**. The code's current `form` / `derived_form` / `FormKind` / `DerivedFormState` names are retired in favor of `derivation` / derivation type / state; the rename is in scope here (Story 0). \"Form\" does not appear in new work.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:28:`tool_call_summary` is **removed** (see Scope). Tool-call arguments render as-is; only tool *results* are summarized.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:55:After this epic, every derivation has a deterministic floor and a uniform recovery cascade, so a not-ready or failed derivation degrades to an honest cruder rendering instead of blocking the operation or leaving a hole. Smart compact and turn construction always produce a usable result; only canonical source corruption stops them. Every fallback is recorded through a new logging surface so operators can see, query, and act on derivation health without runtime noise. Prompt smoothing gains a deterministic cleaning floor and a length gate; tool results split cleanly into deterministic full-band truncation and inference smooth-band summaries with per-tool guidance; the dead `tool_call_summary` type is removed; and runtime model/effort changes are recorded as typed blocks instead of opaque notes. The codebase is renamed from `form` to `derivation` throughout.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:76:- Rename `form` / `derived_form` / `FormKind` / `DerivedFormState` to `derivation` / derivation type / state across code and schema.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:80:- Removal of the `tool_call_summary` derivation type.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:82:- Typed runtime-change blocks (`model_change`, `thinking_level_change`) replacing flattened `runtime_note` text for those events.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:89:- pi-lhc consumption of typed runtime blocks for session restoration (the consumer side lives in the pi-lhc PRD; this epic only records and projects them).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:96:| A1 | Epics 02/03/05 derivation pipeline, states, work queue, and deterministic provider are green and stable | Validated | this session | Confirmed against current `lhc` |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:232:**AC-2.5:** The `tool_call_summary` derivation type is removed; tool-call arguments render as-is wherever a tool call appears.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:234:- **TC-2.5a:** No tool_call_summary derivation\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:237:  - Then: no `tool_call_summary` derivation exists or is queued\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:485:Runtime changes that occur mid-thread — model switches and thinking-level switches — are recorded as typed blocks (`model_change`, `thinking_level_change`) carrying structured fields, instead of being flattened into opaque `runtime_note` text. They are recorded at intake and projected as typed blocks; they are placed verbatim in constructed turns (Flow 3). Consumption of these blocks for host session restoration is out of scope (pi-lhc).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:592:8. **Rename mechanics:** scope of the `form`→`derivation` rename across schema, types, work-queue kinds, and tests; whether any persisted schema identifiers change.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:602:**Boundary / risk notes:** wide mechanical rename (`form`→`derivation`, `FormKind`→derivation type, `DerivedFormState`→state) touching schema, types, work-queue kinds, and tests; plus the new logging table and write method. Needs focused tests for the logging surface (levels stored, shared write, query, contained failure) and a green typecheck/test pass proving the rename did not change behavior.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:622:**Delivers:** the full-band truncation / smooth-band summary split with tiered targets and per-tool guidance; removal of `tool_call_summary`.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:658:**Boundary / risk notes:** intake/projection work, not derivation; consumer-side restoration is pi-lhc and out of scope; can land independently of Stories 1–4.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:14:This epic is a **delta over that working system**, not a new build. The recovery cascade it describes is *substantially already present*: `composeRenderingInput` already resolves each component to its ready form or a deterministic fallback and records a `DependencyGap`; `truncateForFallback` already floors tool activity; the work queue already lands `failed`/`blocked` with reasons; the sweep already does report→classify→requeue. The work here is to **complete, correct, and make observable** what exists:\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:16:1. **Rename** `form`→`derivation` across code and schema (the vocabulary is now settled).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:18:3. **Split tool-result rendering** explicitly into deterministic-truncation (full band) vs inference-summary (smooth band) with tiered targets, and **remove `tool_call_summary`** (a derivation type that exists but is being dropped).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:21:6. **Type runtime changes** as `model_change`/`thinking_level_change` blocks instead of flat `runtime_note`.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:65:| `shared/derivation.ts` | MODIFY | Story 0: rename `FormKind`→`DerivationType`, `DerivedForm`→`Derivation`, `DerivedFormState`→`DerivationState`, `derived_form`→`derivation` (schema). Story 2: remove `tool_call_summary` from the kind set | rename (S0), AC-2.5 (S2) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:68:| `tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts` | MODIFY | Drop `tool_call_summary` from `WorkKind`/registry/`LEGACY_KIND_FORMS`; no mechanics change | AC-2.5 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:71:| `domains/turns/internal/compose.ts` | MODIFY | Remove `tool_call_summary` from `PART_PLANS`; cascade write-back; emit fallback log events | AC-2.5, AC-3.1–3.8 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:79:| `providers/deterministic.ts` | MODIFY | Drop `summarizeToolCall` op (follows `tool_call_summary` removal) | AC-2.5 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:89:`form`→`derivation` touches types (`FormKind`→`DerivationType`, `DerivedForm`→`Derivation`, `DerivedFormState`→`DerivationState`, `DerivedFormMetadata`→`DerivationMetadata`, `FormReportEntry`→`DerivationReportEntry`, `HandlerFormWrite`→`HandlerDerivationWrite`), the `derived_form` table → `derivation`, the column `form` → `derivation_type`, and every reference. This is a migration (v7): the table/column rename runs in `shared/storage.ts` migration. The existing suite is the rename's safety net — behavior is unchanged, so green-after-rename is the gate (Story 0). The rename keeps `tool_call_summary` *in* the kind set (just renamed `DerivationType`); its **removal is Story 2's** (AC-2.5), where it is dropped from the kind set, the work-queue registry, `LEGACY_KIND_FORMS`, `PART_PLANS`, the provider interface, and the deterministic provider. Splitting it this way keeps Story 0 behavior-preserving and gives the removal its own red/green in its owning story.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:153:// was FormKind / FORM_KINDS — tool_call_summary removed\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:166:export interface Derivation {          // was DerivedForm\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:169:  derivationType: DerivationType;      // was `form`\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:308:- **Migration/compatibility:** the v7 rename migration; existing suite green post-rename; `tool_call_summary` removal has its own coverage.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:315:Reuse the existing tiers (`red-verify` / `verify` / `green-verify` / `verify-all`); no new scripts. Story 0's rename is mechanically behavior-preserving — the existing suite green under the renamed vocabulary is its gate. The `tool_call_summary` removal is Story 2's (AC-2.5), a real behavior/schema change with its own red/green there. Recovery stories gate on `verify`. The provider doubles (`failingProvider`, `probingProvider`, `spyProvider`) live in `test/` fixtures alongside the existing deterministic provider.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:328:8. **Rename mechanics:** v7 migration renames table/column; types renamed across the tree (Story 0). `tool_call_summary` is renamed-but-retained in Story 0 and **removed in Story 2** (AC-2.5), so the rename stays behavior-preserving and the removal gets its own coverage (DD-1).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:336:| 0 | Foundation: v7 rename migration + `tech-utils/logging` (rename retains `tool_call_summary`; its removal is Story 2) | Red (rename compiles; log surface skeleton) → Green (suite passes under renamed vocabulary; log tests pass). Rename is mechanically behavior-preserving. |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:338:| 2 | Tool-result tiers + `tool_call_summary` removal | Red → Green |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:350:- pi-lhc consumption of typed runtime blocks for session restoration.\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:150:      validEvent(\"runtime_note\"),\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:339:// Chunk 0's named architecture risk — row + pending form + poke all drop on\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:427:describe(\"architecture-risk: enqueue atomicity — row, pending form, poke commit or vanish together\", () => {\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:451:    // prompt's form, two for the turn's rendering + projection.\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:459:  it(\"an induced rollback after enqueue drops the work row, the pending form row, and the poke\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:530:  it(\"re-enqueueing at a later source version resets the form row to pending at that version\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/report-repair.test.ts:143:// ── the mixed-state thread: every form state landed for real ─────\npackages/lhc/test/report-repair.test.ts:180:describe(\"TC-4.1 / AC-4.1: every landed form reads back in exactly one of the four states\", () => {\npackages/lhc/test/report-repair.test.ts:198:    // the form at e