ge.ts:182:  `DELETE FROM work_item WHERE kind = 'tool_call_summary';`,\npackages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:183:  `DELETE FROM derivation WHERE subject_kind = 'message' AND derivation_type = 'tool_call_summary';`,\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:25:  readDerivedForms,\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:45:  if (!created.ok) throw new Error(`thread creation failed: ${created.error.reason}`);\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:64:  if (!result.ok) throw new Error(`batch failed: ${result.error.reason}`);\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:70:  if (!result.ok) throw new Error(`drain failed: ${result.error.reason}`);\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:84:  return readDerivedForms(filePath).find(\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:89:describe(\"TC-2.1 / AC-2.1: prompt smoothing lands a ready form readable alongside the message\", () => {\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:90:  it(\"intake a prompt, drain → smoothed form ready with the double's deterministic output\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:106:    // (02F-001): listMessages carries the stored form on the message record —\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:219:describe(\"TC-2.6 / AC-2.6: provider exhaustion lands the form failed; the message stays readable\", () => {\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:220:  it(\"smoothing exhausts the retry budget → form failed with the provider's reason; read-back unaffected\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:241:    const form = formOf(filePath, \"m1\", \"smoothed_prompt\");\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:242:    expect(form?.state).toBe(\"failed\");\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:243:    expect(form?.reason).toBe(\"scripted exhaustion (smoothPrompt)\");\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:244:    expect(form?.content).toBeUndefined();\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:254:describe(\"TC-2.7 / AC-2.7: kinds with no derivable form queue no work and carry no state rows\", () => {\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:260:    // assistant_thinking joins the no-derivable-form kinds (Fix 3.2 coverage):\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:265:      validEvent(\"runtime_note\"),\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:274:    expect(readDerivedForms(filePath)).toEqual([]);\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:291:    expect(readDerivedForms(filePath).map((f) => f.derivationType)).toEqual([\npackages/lhc/src/shared/errors.ts:18:  | \"provider_failure\" // system_error — exhausted retries; form.reason carries detail\npackages/lhc/src/shared/errors.ts:19:  | \"source_damaged\" // state_corruption — handler found corrupt source; form blocked\npackages/lhc/src/shared/errors.ts:20:  // Epic 03 (tech design §Interface Definitions): the surface-skeleton stub\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:14:This epic is a **delta over that working system**, not a new build. The recovery cascade it describes is *substantially already present*: `composeRenderingInput` already resolves each component to its ready form or a deterministic fallback and records a `DependencyGap`; `truncateForFallback` already floors tool activity; the work queue already lands `failed`/`blocked` with reasons; the sweep already does report→classify→requeue. The work here is to **complete, correct, and make observable** what exists:\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:16:1. **Rename** `form`→`derivation` across code and schema (the vocabulary is now settled).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:18:3. **Split tool-result rendering** explicitly into deterministic-truncation (full band) vs inference-summary (smooth band) with tiered targets, and **remove `tool_call_summary`** (a derivation type that exists but is being dropped).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:21:6. **Type runtime changes** as `model_change`/`thinking_level_change` blocks instead of flat `runtime_note`.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:27:The only external boundary is `DerivationProvider` (`shared/derivation.ts`). Tests run everything else real — real temp SQLite per the persistence/atomicity/idempotency contracts — and substitute the provider through the existing `createDeterministicProvider()` (`providers/deterministic.ts`), whose output is marked and input-derived so in-process and spawned runs are byte-identical. New recovery tests reuse it plus a **failing/slow provider double** to exercise terminal-failure and retryable paths. Nothing else is mocked.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:65:| `shared/derivation.ts` | MODIFY | Story 0: rename `FormKind`→`DerivationType`, `DerivedForm`→`Derivation`, `DerivedFormState`→`DerivationState`, `derived_form`→`derivation` (schema). Story 2: remove `tool_call_summary` from the kind set | rename (S0), AC-2.5 (S2) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:68:| `tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts` | MODIFY | Drop `tool_call_summary` from `WorkKind`/registry/`LEGACY_KIND_FORMS`; no mechanics change | AC-2.5 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:71:| `domains/turns/internal/compose.ts` | MODIFY | Remove `tool_call_summary` from `PART_PLANS`; cascade write-back; emit fallback log events | AC-2.5, AC-3.1–3.8 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:79:| `providers/deterministic.ts` | MODIFY | Drop `summarizeToolCall` op (follows `tool_call_summary` removal) | AC-2.5 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:89:`form`→`derivation` touches types (`FormKind`→`DerivationType`, `DerivedForm`→`Derivation`, `DerivedFormState`→`DerivationState`, `DerivedFormMetadata`→`DerivationMetadata`, `FormReportEntry`→`DerivationReportEntry`, `HandlerFormWrite`→`HandlerDerivationWrite`), the `derived_form` table → `derivation`, the column `form` → `derivation_type`, and every reference. This is a migration (v7): the table/column rename runs in `shared/storage.ts` migration. The existing suite is the rename's safety net — behavior is unchanged, so green-after-rename is the gate (Story 0). The rename keeps `tool_call_summary` *in* the kind set (just renamed `DerivationType`); its **removal is Story 2's** (AC-2.5), where it is dropped from the kind set, the work-queue registry, `LEGACY_KIND_FORMS`, `PART_PLANS`, the provider interface, and the deterministic provider. Splitting it this way keeps Story 0 behavior-preserving and gives the removal its own red/green in its owning story.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:153:// was FormKind / FORM_KINDS — tool_call_summary removed\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:166:export interface Derivation {          // was DerivedForm\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:169:  derivationType: DerivationType;      // was `form`\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:308:- **Migration/compatibility:** the v7 rename migration; existing suite green post-rename; `tool_call_summary` removal has its own coverage.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:315:Reuse the existing tiers (`red-verify` / `verify` / `green-verify` / `verify-all`); no new scripts. Story 0's rename is mechanically behavior-preserving — the existing suite green under the renamed vocabulary is its gate. The `tool_call_summary` removal is Story 2's (AC-2.5), a real behavior/schema change with its own red/green there. Recovery stories gate on `verify`. The provider doubles (`failingProvider`, `probingProvider`, `spyProvider`) live in `test/` fixtures alongside the existing deterministic provider.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:328:8. **Rename mechanics:** v7 migration renames table/column; types renamed across the tree (Story 0). `tool_call_summary` is renamed-but-retained in Story 0 and **removed in Story 2** (AC-2.5), so the rename stays behavior-preserving and the removal gets its own coverage (DD-1).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:336:| 0 | Foundation: v7 rename migration + `tech-utils/logging` (rename retains `tool_call_summary`; its removal is Story 2) | Red (rename compiles; log surface skeleton) → Green (suite passes under renamed vocabulary; log tests pass). Rename is mechanically behavior-preserving. |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:338:| 2 | Tool-result tiers + `tool_call_summary` removal | Red → Green |\npackages/lhc/test/threads-a8.test.ts:6:// only through the connector (anti-shim: the scope is the query, not a filter\npackages/lhc/test/threads-a8.test.ts:28:  if (!result.ok) throw new Error(`create failed: ${result.error.reason}`);\npackages/lhc/test/report-repair.test.ts:34:  readDerivedForms,\npackages/lhc/test/report-repair.test.ts:56:  if (!created.ok) throw new Error(`thread creation failed: ${created.error.reason}`);\npackages/lhc/test/report-repair.test.ts:81:  if (!result.ok) throw new Error(`batch failed: ${result.error.reason}`);\npackages/lhc/test/report-repair.test.ts:91:  if (!result.ok) throw new Error(`drain failed: ${result.error.reason}`);\npackages/lhc/test/report-repair.test.ts:96:  return readDerivedForms(filePath).find(\npackages/lhc/test/report-repair.test.ts:139:  if (!result.ok) throw new Error(`${owner} report failed: ${result.error.reason}`);\npackages/lhc/test/report-repair.test.ts:143:// ── the mixed-state thread: every form state landed for real ─────\npackages/lhc/test/report-repair.test.ts:180:describe(\"TC-4.1 / AC-4.1: every landed form reads back in exactly one of the four states\", () => {\npackages/lhc/test/report-repair.test.ts:198:    // the form at exhaustion (DD-1: the queue row is gone; this is durable).\npackages/lhc/test/report-repair.test.ts:2