ion|chunk derivation|compact recovery|Chunk Derivation|compactRecovery|chunk\\\" docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery packages/lhc -S'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:443:    chunkPolicy:\\npackages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:444:      config.chunkPolicy ?? { targetProjectedTokens: 2200, maxProjectedTokens: 4400 },\\npackages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:466:  requirePositive(resolved.chunkPolicy.targetProjectedTokens, \\\"chunkPolicy.targetProjectedTokens\\\");\\npackages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:467:  if (resolved.chunkPolicy.maxProjectedTokens < resolved.chunkPolicy.targetProjectedTokens) {\\npackages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:469:      \\\"createSdk config: chunkPolicy.maxProjectedTokens must be >= targetProjectedTokens\\\",\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/team-impl-log.md:23:5. 04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery — Story 4: Chunk Derivation and Compact Recovery\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/team-impl-log.md:89:- Test files: smoothing-recovery, tool-result-rendering, turn-cascade, chunk-compact-recovery, logging-surface, runtime-change-typing\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/team-impl-log.md:208:- Current Story: `04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery`\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/team-impl-log.md:214:- Validation Artifact: `artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/001-story-validate.json`\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/test-plan.md:83:### Flow 4 — Chunk Derivation and Compact Recovery → `test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts`\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/test-plan.md:87:| TC-4.1a | 4.1 | chunk closes | detailed + brief = two separate work items |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/test-plan.md:96:| TC-4.7a | 4.7 | compact falls back to concat | log entry: chunk, derivation type, reason, fallback |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/test-plan.md:97:| TC-4.8a | 4.8 | background chunk summary, member `lower_band_projection` `pending` | summary work requeues (waits) with reason `member_projection_not_ready` — not concat, not `failed`, not a provider-failure reason |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/test-plan.md:147:| 4 — chunk/compact recovery | background-wait + compact stored-member concat fallback (no model) tests red | TC-4.1a–4.8b pass |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:15:**Vocabulary (this epic settles it).** A **derivation** is the stored result of producing a representation of existing content — a smoothed prompt, a tool-result summary, a turn rendering, a chunk summary. To **derive** is the act. A **derivation type** names which one. A derivation carries a **state**. The code's current `form` / `derived_form` / `FormKind` / `DerivedFormState` names are retired in favor of `derivation` / derivation type / state; the rename is in scope here (Story 0). \\\"Form\\\" does not appear in new work.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:24:| `lower_band_projection` | turn | composition | detailed-chunk input; fallback under turn rendering |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:25:| `chunk_summary_detailed` | chunk | inference | detailed band |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:26:| `chunk_summary_brief` | chunk | inference | brief band |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:37:Two things stay clean, one thing stays honest. The **canonical subject** (the message/turn/chunk content) carries no degraded/fallback marker. A **recovered `ready` output** carries no marker either — how it got there (full, floored, or original) is not a distinction the consumer branches on, and there is no \\\"degraded\\\" state. But the **derivation record itself keeps its real state and reason**: a `failed` or `blocked` derivation stays `failed`/`blocked` with its failure reason, inspectable through health (Epic 04). Fallback *events* are log-only; derivation *state* is not — the two are different channels. There is no extra field on the subject or the ready output.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:64:- [Chunk Derivation and Compact Recovery](#4-chunk-derivation-and-compact-recovery) — chunk summaries; stored-member concat fallback at compact (no model); corruption blocks. AC: 4.1–4.8\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:98:| A3 | `lower_band_projection` already exists as turn-derivation's second output and the chunk-detailed input | Unvalidated | Tech Lead | Confirm-and-document pass; likely no new work |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:355:### 4. Chunk Derivation and Compact Recovery\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:357:A closed chunk derives two independent summaries — `chunk_summary_detailed` and `chunk_summary_brief` — each with its own state, from the chunk's member turns (via `lower_band_projection`). Smart compact assembles a view from band materials and **never calls a model**. When a needed chunk summary is not ready at compact time, compact does not re-derive it; it falls back to a **deterministic concatenation** of the member content uncompressed — more detail, never a hole. Healing of the summary itself happens out-of-band: the readiness sweep (which runs before compact) requeues transient failures, the background drain produces the real summary, and the next compact uses it. Compact surfaces warnings the user can see and can stop. Only canonical source corruption blocks a compact; missing derivations degrade.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:359:1. A chunk closes; detailed and brief summaries are queued as independent work items\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:360:2. Smart compact assembles bands from chunk summaries and turn renderings\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:366:**AC-4.1:** A closed chunk's detailed and brief summaries are derived as two independent work items with independent states.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:369:  - Given: a chunk closes\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:377:**AC-4.2:** At compact, a chunk summary that is not ready (`pending` or `failed`) resolves through `turns.compactChunkMaterial` to a deterministic stored-member concatenation; compact makes no provider call and does not re-derive the summary.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:384:**AC-4.3:** When a chunk summary still cannot be made ready, compact falls back to a deterministic concatenation of the chunk's member content (uncompressed) rather than leaving a gap.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:387:  - Given: a chunk summary that is not ready at compact time\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:394:  - Given: a compact performs a chunk-summary fallback\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:405:  - Given: multiple missing/failed chunk summaries\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:409:  - Given: canonical source for a chunk's turns is corrupt\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:413:**AC-4.6:** Smart compact performs no provider calls at all; background chunk derivation performs no provider work inside a DB write transaction.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:416:  - Given: a compact over a thread with not-ready chunk summaries, provider spy installed\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:423:  - Given: a compact falls back to concatenation for a chunk\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:425:  - Then: a log entry records the chunk, derivation type, reason, and fallback\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:427:**AC-4.8:** Background chunk-summary derivation behaves differently from compact-time recovery when a member `lower_band_projection` is not ready: because no consumer is waiting, it **requeues and waits** for the input rather than concatenating or failing. It blocks (no progress) only on source corruption of a member; a not-ready member input degrades to a requeue, never a hole or a terminal failure.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:430:  - Given: a chunk summary derives in the background while a member `lower_band_projection` is `pending`\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:432:  - Then: the chunk summary work requeues (waits) rather than concatenating or landing `failed`\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:435:  - When: the background chunk summary attempts to derive\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:458:**AC-5.3:** A fallback *event* is recorded only in the log. The canonical subject (message/turn/chunk content) and any `ready` derivation output carry no degraded/fallback marker. This does not erase derivation state: a `failed` or `blocked` derivation keeps its state and reason on its own record (inspectable per Epic 04) — that is the derivation's state channel, distinct from the fallback-event log channel.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:551:| subjectId | string | no | The subject (message/turn/chunk) id, when relevant |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:587:3. **Background chunk-summary requeue mechanics:** AC-4.8 decides the behavior (requeue/wait on a not-ready member input; block only on member source corruption). Tech design settles the mechanics: requeue backoff, how member source corruption is detected, and how a waiting chunk summary is re-triggered when its member input lands ready.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:588:4. **`lower_band_projection` standalone:** confirm and document it as turn-derivation's second output and the chunk-detailed input; likely no new work, needs a confirm pass.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:642:### Story 4: Chunk derivation and compact recovery\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:644:**Delivers:** independent detailed/brief chunk summaries and a smart compact that regenerates-or-concatenates, warns, is stoppable, and blocks only on source corruption.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:645:**Governing idea:** the cascade instantiated at the chunk/compact level — more detail on fallback, never a hole, corruption is the only stop.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:647:**Boundary / risk notes:** the background chunk-summary requeue behavior is decided (AC-4.8); its mechanics (backoff, re-trigger on member ready, source-corruption detection) are settled in tech design (TD Q3). User-visible warning + stop straddles the LHC/pi-lhc boundary (Flow 5 / TD Q6).\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:678:- [x] Stories sequence logically (foundation → production floors → turn cascade → chunk/compact cascade → parity)\\npackages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/index.ts:7:import { chunkBriefV1 } from \\\"./chunk-brief-v1.js\\\";\\npackages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/index.ts:8:import { chunkDetailedV1 } from \\\"./chunk-detailed-v1.js\\\";\\npackages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/index.ts:27:  [chunkDetailedV1.name]: chunkDetailedV1,\\npackages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/index.ts:28:  [chunkBriefV1.name]: chunkBriefV1,\\npackages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/index.ts:43:  chunk_summary_detailed: chunkDetailedV1.name,\\npackages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/index.ts:44:  chunk_summary_brief: chunkBriefV1.name,\\npackages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/chunk-detailed-v1.ts:13:export const chunkDetailedV1: PromptTemplate<{\\npackages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/chunk-detailed-v1.ts:17:  name: \\\"chunk-detailed-v1\\\",\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/coverage.md:63:| Chunk close | Closed chunks queue detailed and brief summaries independently | Story 4 | TC-4.1a, TC-4.1b |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/coverage.md:67:| Background chunk waiting | Not-ready member `lower_band_projection` requeues; member source corruption surfaces | Story 4 | TC-4.8a, TC-4.8b |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/coverage.md:80:| Story 4 | repair / recovery | Compact uses stored band material or deterministic member concatenation, never a model call, and blocks only on canonical source corruption. | compact recovery plus background summary waiting behavior | degraded-state scoping, active path/source path selection, command context, thread-view/turns boundary | Keep because both compact fallback and background waiting enforce the same chunk/source corruption boundary. |\\npackages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/chunk-brief-v1.ts:14:export const chunkBriefV1: PromptTemplate<{\\npackages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/chunk-brief-v1.ts:18:  name: \\\"chunk-brief-v1\\\",\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:1:# Story 4: Chunk Derivation and Compact Recovery\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:6:Derive independent chunk summaries and make smart compact fall back to deterministic stored-member concatenation without provider calls.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:13:**Objective:** instantiate recovery at chunk and compact level so compact produces usable band material with warnings and blocks only on canonical source corruption.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:16:- Independent `chunk_summary_detailed` and `chunk_summary_brief` work items and states.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:17:- Smart compact recovery through `turns.compactChunkMaterial`.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:21:- Background chunk-summary requeue/wait behavior for not-ready member `lower_band_projection`.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:33:**AC-4.1:** A closed chunk's detailed and brief summaries are derived as two independent work items with independent states.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:36:  - Given: a chunk closes\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:44:**AC-4.2:** At compact, a chunk summary that is not ready (`pending` or `failed`) resolves through `turns.compactChunkMaterial` to a deterministic stored-member concatenation; compact makes no provider call and does not re-derive the summary.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:51:**AC-4.3:** When a chunk summary still cannot be made ready, compact falls back to a deterministic concatenation of the chunk's member content (uncompressed) rather than leaving a gap.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:54:  - Given: a chunk summary that is not ready at compact time\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:61:  - Given: a compact performs a chunk-summary fallback\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:72:  - Given: multiple missing/failed chunk summaries\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:76:  - Given: canonical source for a chunk's turns is corrupt\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:80:**AC-4.6:** Smart compact performs no provider calls at all; background chunk derivation performs no provider work inside a DB write transaction.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:83:  - Given: a compact over a thread with not-ready chunk summaries, provider spy installed\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:90:  - Given: a compact falls back to concatenation for a chunk\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:92:  - Then: a log entry records the chunk, derivation type, reason, and fallback\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:94:**AC-4.8:** Background chunk-summary derivation behaves differently from compact-time recovery when a member `lower_band_projection` is not ready: because no consumer is waiting, it **requeues and waits** for the input rather than concatenating or failing. It blocks (no progress) only on source corruption of a member; a not-ready member input degrades to a requeue, never a hole or a terminal failure.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:97:  - Given: a chunk summary derives in the background while a member `lower_band_projection` is `pending`\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:99:  - Then: the chunk summary work requeues (waits) rather than concatenating or landing `failed`\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:102:  - When: the background chunk summary attempts to derive\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:110:Story 4 owns the chunk and compact recovery boundary. Background chunk-summary derivation waits for member `lower_band_projection` inputs because no consumer is waiting. Compact is a consumer path and never calls a provider; it asks the turns surface for ready summary material or deterministic stored-member concatenation.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:131:| Background chunk summary | `packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/chunks.ts` |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:133:| Chunk fallback assembly | `packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/chunk-recovery.ts` (NEW per tech design) |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:137:| Story tests | `packages/lhc/test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts` (planned) |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:145:- [tech-design.md §Compact chunk material interface](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:226), lines 226-236\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:146:- [tech-design.md §Compact chunk material mechanics](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:283), lines 283-295\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:154:| TC-4.1a | `packages/lhc/test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts` | Chunk close queues detailed and brief summaries as separate work items. |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:155:| TC-4.1b | `packages/lhc/test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts` | Detailed and brief summary states can diverge independently. |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:156:| TC-4.2a | `packages/lhc/test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts` | Failed detailed summary at compact returns stored-member concat through `compactChunkMaterial` and zero provider calls. |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:157:| TC-4.3a | `packages/lhc/test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts` | Unready summary yields deterministic concat band entry with no missing span. |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:158:| TC-4.4a | `packages/lhc/test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts` | Compact fallback emits visible warning naming what fell back. |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:159:| TC-4.4b | `packages/lhc/test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts` | Stop request during fallback assembly halts without corrupting thread. |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:160:| TC-4.5a | `packages/lhc/test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts` | Multiple missing/failed summaries complete compact with concat fallbacks. |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:161:| TC-4.5b | `packages/lhc/test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts` | Corrupt canonical source makes `compactChunkMaterial` return blocked and compact refuse with `state_corruption`. |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:162:| TC-4.6a | `packages/lhc/test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts` | Compact over not-ready summaries records zero provider calls for the entire compact. |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:163:| TC-4.7a | `packages/lhc/test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts` | Compact concat fallback writes log entry with chunk, derivation type, reason, and fallback. |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:164:| TC-4.8a | `packages/lhc/test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts` | Background chunk summary requeues with `member_projection_not_ready`, not concat/failed/provider failure. |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:165:| TC-4.8b | `packages/lhc/test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts` | Member turn source corruption surfaces instead of looping or fabricating. |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:171:| Compact makes no provider call | `packages/lhc/test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts` | `spyProvider` observes zero calls through full compact path with not-ready summaries. | Helper-level concat tests would not prove compact avoids provider work. |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:173:| Dependency-wait classification | `packages/lhc/test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts` | Not-ready member projection requeues with `member_projection_not_ready`. | A generic retry test can misclassify normal dependency waiting as provider failure. |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:174:| Idempotent background wait | `packages/lhc/test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts` | Requeue-and-wait does not duplicate work items across retries. | Single-run checks do not prove retry stability. |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:175:| Corruption blocks | `packages/lhc/test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts` | Canonical source corruption blocks compact while missing derivations degrade. | Fallback tests alone can accidentally fabricate corrupt source content. |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:179:- Compact never calls a model/provider. Not-ready chunk summaries compact through `turns.compactChunkMaterial(...)` to stored-member concat; healing is sweep plus background drain plus next compact.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:193:- Registration/default path: snapshot calls public `domains/turns/index.ts` `compactChunkMaterial(...)` for not-ready chunk summaries.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:194:- Evidence: `packages/lhc/test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts` runs compact with `spyProvider` and `cd packages/lhc && pnpm run boundaries` proves thread-view uses the turns surface, never internals.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:198:- Targeted: `cd packages/lhc && pnpm run test -- test/chunk-compact-recovery.test.ts`\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery.md:213:- Background chunk-summary derivation requeues on not-ready member `lower_band_projection`.\\npackages/lhc/src/inference/adapter.ts:116:    summarizeChunkDetailed: (i) => callKind(\\\"chunk_summary_detailed\\\", i),\\npackages/lhc/src/inference/adapter.ts:117:    summarizeChunkBrief: (i) => callKind(\\\"chunk_summary_brief\\\", i),\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/00-foundation.md:43:**AC-5.3:** A fallback *event* is recorded only in the log. The canonical subject (message/turn/chunk content) and any `ready` derivation output carry no degraded/fallback marker. This does not erase derivation state: a `failed` or `blocked` derivation keeps its state and reason on its own record (inspectable per Epic 04) — that is the derivation's state channel, distinct from the fallback-event log channel.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:12:Epics 02/03/05 built and shipped the derivation pipeline: the work queue with version-checked completion and terminal failure (`tech-utils/work-queue`), the four-state derivation vocabulary (`shared/derivation.ts`), message-level handlers, turn composition (`domains/turns/internal/compose.ts`), chunk mechanics (`chunks.ts`), and the readiness sweep (`domains/thread-view/internal/sweep.ts`). All green.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:20:5. **Define background vs compact chunk recovery** (requeue-and-wait vs stored-member concat fallback — compact calls no model).\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:23:Two disciplines, inherited and reinforced. **No provider work inside a DB write transaction**, and **no provider work at all on the intake/serving hot paths** — turn-construction recovery that re-derives runs its provider call outside the completion transaction, exactly as the existing handlers do. **And compact calls no model at all** (Epic 03 invariant: compact assembles stored artifacts; the sweep, which runs before it, is the only thing that requeues). This epic does not change that: compact-time chunk recovery is *concat-from-stored-members only*, never an inline provider call. Healing of a not-ready chunk summary happens through the existing sweep + background drain, then the next compact picks up the healed artifact — not by compact re-deriving inline.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:41:    WQ --> TH[turns handlers: derive / chunks]\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:73:| `domains/turns/internal/chunks.ts` | MODIFY | Background chunk-summary requeue-and-wait on not-ready member input (reason `member_projection_not_ready`) | AC-4.1, AC-4.8 |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:75:| `domains/turns/internal/chunk-recovery.ts` | NEW | Pure: assemble a chunk's band entry from stored member content when its summary is not ready (concat, no model) | AC-4.2–4.4, AC-4.7 |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:131:### DD-6: Background chunk recovery waits; compact recovery concats from stored members (no model)\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:135:- **Background** (`chunks.ts` / chunk-summary handler): a chunk summary whose member `lower_band_projection` is not ready **requeues and waits** — no consumer is waiting, so deferring until the input lands is correct. Mechanically: the handler, finding a not-ready member input, returns retryable with reason **`member_projection_not_ready`** (a dependency-not-ready reason, *not* `provider_unavailable` — the review's #5: a health report must not misclassify normal dependency waiting as provider failure). The existing backoff requeues it; member source corruption returns `blocked`.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:136:- **Compact** (`turns.compactChunkMaterial`, called from `snapshot.ts`): a not-ready chunk summary resolves to a **deterministic concatenation of the chunk's stored member content** (uncompressed) — no provider call, honoring the Epic 03 \\\"compact never calls a model\\\" invariant. Compact emits a visible warning, is stoppable, and blocks only on canonical source corruption of the span (`state_corruption`, existing). Healing of the summary itself happens out-of-band: the sweep (which runs before compact) requeues transient failures, the background drain produces the real summary, and the *next* compact uses it. Compact never re-derives inline.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:144:Compact (AC-4.6) is simpler than the prior draft claimed: it makes **no provider call at all** (DD-6), so there is no across-provider-transaction concern — its chunk recovery is a pure stored-member concat. The AC-4.6 test therefore asserts the stronger property directly: a compact over not-ready summaries observes **zero provider calls**.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:159:  \\\"chunk_summary_detailed\\\",\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:160:  \\\"chunk_summary_brief\\\",\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:226:### Compact chunk material (`domains/turns/index.ts` surface op — no provider)\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:229:// Returns the ready chunk summary if present, else a deterministic\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:230:// concatenation of the chunk's stored member content. NEVER calls a provider\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:232:export function compactChunkMaterial(ctx: OperationContext, chunkId: string):\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:283:### Compact chunk material (`turns.compactChunkMaterial`, called from `snapshot.ts`) — no provider\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:286:for each chunk summary needed by the band plan:\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:287:    m = turns.compactChunkMaterial(ctx, chunkId)              # surface op, NO provider call\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:306:- **Idempotency/retry:** background chunk requeue-and-wait does not duplicate work (existing `hasLiveItem`/version scoping); the wait reason is `member_projection_not_ready`, not a provider-failure reason, so health classification stays correct.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:323:3. **Background chunk floor:** DD-6 — requeue-and-wait with reason `member_projection_not_ready` (not `provider_unavailable`), block only on member source corruption.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:324:4. **`lower_band_projection` standalone:** confirmed via `LEGACY_KIND_FORMS` and `compose`/`chunks` — it is turn-derivation's second output and the chunk-detailed input. No new work; documented in DD-6.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:332:## Work Breakdown (chunks)\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:343:Detailed TC→test mapping and per-chunk Red/Green exit criteria are in `test-plan.md`.\\npackages/lhc/src/shared/derivation.ts:12:export type SubjectKind = \\\"message\\\" | \\\"turn\\\" | \\\"chunk\\\";\\npackages/lhc/src/shared/derivation.ts:23:  \\\"chunk_summary_detailed\\\",\\npackages/lhc/src/shared/derivation.ts:24:  \\\"chunk_summary_brief\\\",\\npackages/lhc/src/shared/derivation.ts:60:// from provider prose; stamped on the turn_rendering form so the chunk\\npackages/lhc/src/shared/derivation.ts:151:  // context (the production chunk handlers always pass them).\\npackages/lhc/sr