{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"reviewerLabels\":[\"epic-reviewer-1\",\"epic-reviewer-2\"],\"reconciliationSummary\":\"Both reviewer blockers remain supported by current code and epic evidence. Reviewer 1's over-large tool-result recovery blocker is confirmed because intake/queued handling applies the large-tier truncation rule, while turn-close recovery independently calls summarizeToolResult without the tier gate or summary parameters. Reviewer 2's absent-derivation fallback logging blocker is confirmed because compose records a dependency gap for missing rows but only emits a recovery receipt when a row exists, and derive logs only recovery receipts. The duplicate rename findings are merged as one nonblocking finding. Gates were rerun locally and passed, with real-inference tests skipped because LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY is unset.\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Flows 2 and 3 diverge at consumption-time recovery: the queued tool-result path satisfies over-large tool_result_summary derivations by deterministic truncation, but turn-close recovery reimplements tool-result recovery and can invoke inference for the same tier.\",\"Flow 3 and Flow 5 diverge for absent derivation rows: composition marks a fallback/gap, but the logging path only logs recoveries for existing rows.\",\"No material fake adapter, hidden shim, placeholder provider, or non-real default production path was verified under packages/lhc/src; deterministic providers remain explicit test/config fixtures.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Tech-design DD-3 requires tool results above the large tier to land ready by deterministic truncation with no inference item/provider call; packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:150-196 and packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts:145-159 implement that for intake/queued work, but packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:117-127 bypasses it during recovery.\",\"Tech-design DD-5 and epic AC-3.6/AC-5.3 require fallback events to be logged separately from derivation state; packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts:222-238 omits a RecoveryReceipt when the derivation row is absent, so packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:196-211 has nothing to log.\",\"The form-to-derivation rename is incomplete at the production vocabulary level: schema/shared types are renamed, but production modules still expose form-named files, helpers, constants, and comments.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Story Gate passed locally: cd packages/lhc && pnpm run verify completed with 47 test files passed, 426 tests passed, and 9 skipped.\",\"Epic Gate passed locally: cd packages/lhc && pnpm run verify-all completed with 47 test files passed, 426 tests passed, and 9 skipped.\",\"Coverage remains incomplete for cross-story recovery: tests cover over-large tool results on intake/queued handling and normal composition fallback, but not failed/pending over-large tool_result_summary recovery at turn close.\",\"Coverage remains incomplete for absent derivation-row fallback logging: tests cover pending/failed row fallback logging, but not missing-row fallback logging.\",\"Flow 5/6 logging and runtime-change coverage is otherwise present; Flow 0 rename coverage is partial because stale production vocabulary remains.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:117-127 performs a real provider call for tool_result_summary recovery with raw content, unknown_tool, no targetTokens, and no guidance. For over-large tool results this violates the deterministic truncation/no-inference production invariant.\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts:148-153 correctly defines the tool-result fallback as truncateForFallback, but recoverMessageForms runs before composition and can replace a non-ready row with provider output, preventing the deterministic floor path from being used for over-large sources.\",\"Smart compact was not found to call a provider in the inspected production path; compact resolves chunk material through the turns surface and stored-member concatenation.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"E06-BLOCK-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Turn-close recovery bypasses the tool-result large-tier gate\",\"evidence\":\"The queued handler returns truncateForFallback(content) as ready with no provider call when estimateTokens(content) exceeds largeTierTokens at packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts:145-159; intake also writes the large summary ready and avoids queueing at packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:150-196. Turn-close recovery separately calls run.provider.summarizeToolResult for tool_result_summary at packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:117-127 with raw content, toolName unknown_tool, no targetTokens, and no guidance. This violates AC-2.3, AC-2.7, AC-3.3, and DD-3 for over-large tool results.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.3\",\"AC-2.4\",\"AC-2.7\",\"AC-3.3\",\"DD-3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"E06-BLOCK-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Absent derivation fallback is not logged\",\"evidence\":\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts:222-238 creates a DependencyGap whenever a derivable component falls back, but creates a RecoveryReceipt only when form !== undefined. packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:196-211 logs only recoveries. Therefore an absent smoothed_prompt or tool_result_summary row can render through fallback and record a gap without producing the fallback log entry required by AC-3.6 and AC-5.3.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.6\",\"AC-5.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"E06-NB-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Form-to-derivation rename remains incomplete in production vocabulary\",\"evidence\":\"The epic scope and DD-1 require a total form-to-derivation rename. Current production source still contains form-named APIs and constants, including ComposeFormRow and composeFormKey in packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts:38-49, MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS in packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:135-140, readMessageFormRows in packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/forms.ts:76-108, readOwnedForms in packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/forms.ts:181+, and imports/usages in packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/index.ts:34-37.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/forms.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/forms.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/index.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"Epic Scope: form-to-derivation rename\",\"Story-0\",\"DD-1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E06-NB-002\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Real-inference tests did not run in the gate environment\",\"evidence\":\"Both local gate runs exited 0, but test output reported NOT-RAN: real-inference (LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY unset) and 9 skipped tests.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/test/inference-real.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"Gate Instructions\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Real-inference tests remain skipped in this environment because LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY is unset.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}"}}
